# Per-machine settings for the harness and the skills (docs/dev-setup.md).
# Copy to .claude/local.env (gitignored) and fill in what applies to your
# machine; leave the rest commented out. tools/harness/rs.sh reads it.

# --- Android device running DroidDeck (adb) ---------------------------------
# adb on PATH is used by default. On WSL with the device attached to Windows,
# use Windows' adb.exe (one adb server owns the USB device):
# ADB=/mnt/c/Users/<you>/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk/platform-tools/adb.exe
# ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT=5037
# A DroidDeck checkout with tools/droiddeckctl (default ~/dev/DroidDeck):
# DROIDDECK_DIR=$HOME/dev/DroidDeck
# Root (adb shell su) only makes guest file reads faster; 0 forces the
# DroidDeck-session path:
# SKATE3_ADB_ROOT=0

# --- Game data ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Your own Skate 3 dump (default: <repo>/game):
# SKATE3_GAME_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/games/skate3

# --- Windows A/B (WSL hosts) ------------------------------------------------
# Windows builds are staged on a Windows drive (running from \\wsl.localhost
# is slow), with a test copy of the user data so runs never touch your
# profile:
# SKATE3_WINDOWS_STAGE_ROOT=/mnt/c/Users/<you>/skate3-ab
# SKATE3_WINDOWS_USER_DATA=/mnt/c/Users/<you>/skate3-ab/userdata
# Portable RenderDoc (same version as the device build) for --renderdoc:
# SKATE3_WINDOWS_RENDERDOC=/mnt/c/Users/<you>/tools/RenderDoc_1.46_64

# --- Reverse engineering ------------------------------------------------------
# The Skate 2 debug build's files (names and layouts; never committed):
# SKATE3_RE_REF_DIR=/mnt/c/Users/<you>/Downloads/sk82_TEAM (Jan 17 2009)
